{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For there HaShem confounded the language of all the earth, and from there HaShem scattered them.</b> Know that every place where you find the mention of the special Name inscribed in the letters in reverse order, it indicates the attribute of justice, and this is one of those places. And in many places in the Torah such instances appear, and in each one there is a great reason stated for a necessary and required matter, for it is no accident, but was done with intention and complete providence — when I reach each one I shall rouse you to it and instruct you in its matter and its path. And because He mentioned in the passage ״וירא ה׳ ויאמר ה׳״ — 'And HaShem saw… and HaShem said…' — which is the attribute of mercy, it is hinted to us here that the attribute of justice was stretched out against them to scatter them over the face of all the earth; but it was included in mercy because they were one band, loving one another, as it is written ״שפה אחת ודברים אחדים״ — 'one language and one words' — and therefore He scattered them and did not destroy them entirely like the generation of the Flood. And the reason they were punished with the confounding of language: this was measure for measure, for they sinned through speech, saying ״הבה נבנה לנו עיר״ — 'Come, let us build ourselves a city' — and therefore they were stricken in the power of their speech through the confounding of language. And until now the whole earth had been one language and the entire world spoke in the holy tongue, which is the language through which the world was created, and now that they sinned with their tongue He confounded the languages, and from the descendants of Noah, who were seventy men, the nations separated and from them emerged seventy nations, each to its own language. You already know that seventy princes above guide seventy nations below, and each one of the princes is the root of its nation and its language." "<b>And behold,</b> these princes were the portion of the nations — not so the portion of Jacob, for He is the Maker of all. And just as He is the Elohim of the heavens and the Elohim of elohim, supreme over all, so our language is supreme over all languages, and therefore our Rock and our root, who is the root of the holy tongue, assigned to us the Elohim of Israel. And to this intention our Rabbis of blessed memory explained to us: ״כל השואל צרכיו בלשון ארמי אין מלאכי השרת נזקקים לו״ — 'Whoever asks for his needs in Aramaic, the ministering angels do not attend to him' — ״לפי שאין מלאכי השרת מכירים בלשון ארמי״ — 'because the ministering angels do not recognize the Aramaic language.' And from here one may wonder, for it has already been clarified that the knowledge of the celestial sphere is greater than the knowledge of man, and the knowledge of the angel is greater than the knowledge of the celestial sphere; if so, how is it possible that the ministering angels would not recognize the languages — and behold, Mordecai knew seventy languages, and likewise we find in Joseph the righteous, as our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded on the verse (Psalms 81:6): ״עדות ביהוסף שמו״ — 'He appointed it as a testimony in Joseph' — He added to him one letter from His Name, and through it he knew seventy languages." "<b>Rather,</b> the explanation of this statement of our Rabbis of blessed memory, that they do not recognize the Aramaic language, is with respect to the matter of attending to him; but certainly they do recognize it, only they do not attend to him in another language until he asks in the holy tongue — because they must draw power from those appointed through the holy tongue, which belongs to the Elohim of Israel, and they have no efficacy or power apart from it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:48.615912561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}